xigmatek-connect-lcd (0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * README.md is the overview and the detail lives in docs/ - install.md,
    usage.md, gui.md, themes.md, packaging.md, tools.md, limits.md,
    troubleshooting.md - cut out of the old README by line range rather than
    rewritten, so no measured figure changed on the way.  155 lines of README
    and a nine-row table of where the rest is.

  * The links are checked, because a split is exactly the kind of change that
    breaks a relative path while leaving valid markdown: tools/selftest.sh
    resolves every link in README.md and every docs/*.md (44 of them across ten
    documents), and debian/tests/smoke does the same for the installed layout.

  * docs/screenshot-xigmaui.png, made by tools/screenshot.py: the real window,
    built offscreen the way the suite builds it, with a device path that must
    not exist so that taking the picture never opens anyone's port.

  * The package installs the documents: debian/rules stages them as
    /usr/share/doc/xigmatek-connect-lcd/docs/ because debian/<package>.docs
    installs by basename, and override_dh_compress leaves the markdown and the
    transcripts uncompressed (dh_compress -X.md -X.log) because gzipped ones
    break every relative link in the set.  The images stay out on purpose.

  * Reproducible archives, measured rather than asserted.  debian/changelog's
    0.1 entry was dated ahead of the build that built it, and dpkg-deb pulls
    member mtimes down to SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH while leaving earlier ones alone -
    which is how the published v0.1 asset and a build of the same tree came out
    18 B apart with every file md5 matching.  The 0.1 entry now carries the time
    it was written; the staged trees are touched to the changelog's stamp before
    dh_builddeb; the build job fails if the two packages do not carry exactly
    one member date, equal to that stamp; and a build of 8ac3a32 here and the
    runner's build of 8ac3a32 are the same bytes (5 165 848 B, sha256
    bf887c0eb296c481730a125c8234c6e8584c8f5fb9b69d4f4abb2c46d33fe264).

  * tools/selftest.sh grew with it: the glass-ledger checks read the docs that
    quote the runs, the changelog stamp must not be in the future, the package's
    own __version__ has to agree with pyproject.toml, the PyQt6-absent path is
    checked by hiding PyQt6 behind an import blocker, and the clip-root check
    asserts the rule instead of the state of one machine.  Seventeen offline
    sections, and README, docs/packaging.md, debian/changelog and CI all agree
    on that number.

 -- Tamer Hassan <thameruddin@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 06:54:31 +0200

xigmatek-connect-lcd (0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First packaged form of the project, and the first form that is not a git
    checkout: the display loop (`xigmalcd`), the Qt window (`xigmaui`), the
    three background clips this project vendors, the udev rule, the systemd
    user unit and the menu entry all land in the normal places.
  * The vendor's panel reset ships as its own command, `xigmalcd-reset`,
    because an installed system has no other way back once the panel's
    `logo`/`mode` read 2147483647 - those fields cannot be set over the wire,
    only reset.  It sends nothing without --yes, the shipped unit does not
    arm --allow-reset, and debian/tests/smoke fails if either ever changes.
    tools/reset_panel.py is now the checkout spelling of that same code
    (`xigmalcd/reset.py`) rather than a second copy of it.
  * Data discovery had to become installation-aware first: a path next to the
    checkout is not a thing after `apt install`, so the clip roots are now
    `$XIGMA_MEDIA`, the checkout's `media/` and /usr/share/xigmalcd/media,
    first that exists, with the Windows partition's copies behind them
    (`xigmalcd/main.py:media_roots`).  The window finds its icon the same way:
    the checkout file, then the hicolor copy this package installs.
    tools/selftest.sh checks those rules against fake roots.
  * `xigmatek-connect-lcd-themes` carries ALPHA's own theme library - 27
    `.thm` files as shipped, their decrypted layouts, 44 background clips, 27
    baked overlay PNGs, and the manifest that hashes all 152 entries of the
    125 distinct files they name - copied byte for byte out of the vendor
    installation on the author's bench.  Those bytes are XIGMATEK's, not
    ours, and `debian/copyright` says so instead of pretending to license
    them; the package exists so a user can take them down again in one
    command.
  * Everything measured about the protocol is in `PROTOCOL.md`, and the
    offline suite (`tools/selftest.sh`, seventeen offline sections) is what
    CI runs before it builds a package.

 -- Tamer Hassan <thameruddin@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 05:10:42 +0200
